Pet deathcare is getting digitized

Great news for recently bereaved pet owners: An emerging platform applies A=
mazon-style logistics to pet cremation, ensuring the ashes in your pug's ur=
n aren't from some random corgi.

Angelpaw (https://www.angelpaw.com/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9C799tVRAgjMKbz01_pEgV=
pUarxc5ofszFgCpBv2TlWoWml0vrkm0rnN4osA7MpIM_pLozppLl9JfpwzPGf3jJQY2ZMw&_hsm=
i=3D401714543 ) works with 10k+ vets to cover 100k+ pets per month on the w=
orld's largest pet cremation tracking platform =E2=80=94 essentially Find M=
y Friends for pet remains.

Here's how it works:

- When a pet dies, vets scan a waterproof RFID tag that stores all pet and =
owner data digitally.

- Fixed antennas and handheld scanners track the pet through every cremator=
ium station.

- Owners receive updates at each step, from pickup to when the ashes are re=
ady.

Ruff-ly speaking, how big is its market?

The pet cremation industry has historically run on trust and clipboards =E2=
=80=94 a bit surprising for a $2.4B (https://finance.yahoo.com/news/global-=
pet-cremation-services-market-105500163.html?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9C799tVRAgjMK=
bz01_pEgVpUarxc5ofszFgCpBv2TlWoWml0vrkm0rnN4osA7MpIM_pLozppLl9JfpwzPGf3jJQY=
2ZMw&_hsmi=3D401714543 ) market projected to hit $3.2B by 2032.

Owners often wound up with the wrong ashes: a tough look when 51% (https://=
www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/07/07/about-half-us-of-pet-owners-say-=
their-pets-are-as-much-a-part-of-their-family-as-a-human-member/?_hsenc=3Dp=
2ANqtz-9C799tVRAgjMKbz01_pEgVpUarxc5ofszFgCpBv2TlWoWml0vrkm0rnN4osA7MpIM_pL=
ozppLl9JfpwzPGf3jJQY2ZMw&_hsmi=3D401714543 ) of US pet owners say their pet=
s are as much a part of their family as siblings or parents.

"Pet humanization" offerings =E2=80=94 like premium food, DNA tests, and ve=
terinary telehealth =E2=80=94 are becoming increasingly popular. Angelpaw i=
s a natural extension of that. If we treat pets like family in life, why wo=
uldn't we do so in death?

Other businesses play into that as well:

- CodaPet (https://www.codapet.com/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9C799tVRAgjMKbz01_pEgV=
pUarxc5ofszFgCpBv2TlWoWml0vrkm0rnN4osA7MpIM_pLozppLl9JfpwzPGf3jJQY2ZMw&_hsm=
i=3D401714543 ) is a marketplace connecting families with vets who perform =
in-home euthanasia.

- Obituary Assistant  (https://www.obituary-assistant.com/pets/?_hsenc=3Dp2=
ANqtz-9C799tVRAgjMKbz01_pEgVpUarxc5ofszFgCpBv2TlWoWml0vrkm0rnN4osA7MpIM_pLo=
zppLl9JfpwzPGf3jJQY2ZMw&_hsmi=3D401714543 ) now includes a plug-in for pet =
memorials, letting owners create digital tributes for fallen furry friends =
=E2=80=94 not just human obituaries.

Woof! Any concerns?

Angelpaw is building a data layer on top of 100k monthly pet deaths. That v=
olume could raise eyebrows over data privacy.

And some might find applying Amazon-style logistics to grief unsettling or =
distasteful. Does radical transparency help mourning, or does it industrial=
ize the last intimate act we perform for a pet?

Still, the business case is clear: Americans spent an estimated $157B (http=
s://americanpetproducts.org/industry-trends-and-stats?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9C79=
9tVRAgjMKbz01_pEgVpUarxc5ofszFgCpBv2TlWoWml0vrkm0rnN4osA7MpIM_pLozppLl9Jfpw=
zPGf3jJQY2ZMw&_hsmi=3D401714543 ) on pets in 2025, and death is a life stag=
e we haven't overhauled.

Digitizing the moment all dogs go to heaven could be lucrative.

